-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/10350339109360341","pdf":"","k":["Linguistics","Political science","Sociology","Criminology","History","Geography","Philosophy"]},{"doi":"10.1080/10350339109360342","t":"Television TV by Barney Daniels Tjungurrayi","a":["Anthony Burke"],"d":"1991-01-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/10350339109360342","pdf":"","k":["Media studies","Sociology","Reality tv","Art","Political science","Advertising","Telecommunications","Computer science"]},{"doi":"10.1080/10350339109360332","t":"The dialogic imagination in Tangu myth","a":["Erik Schwimmer"],"d":"1991-01-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/10350339109360332","pdf":"","k":["Dialogic","Mythology","Literature","Art","Aesthetics","Sociology"]},{"doi":"10.1080/10350339109360344","t":"Vico's ancient binarism and problems of social theory today","a":["Alec McHoul"],"d":"1991-01-01","abs":"In this paper, I want to suggest that the difference is ubiquitous - if hidden - and logically insoluble; that any step beyond a state in which there are at least two distinct methodologies in the social sciences is no small order. I want to suggest that it is and has been a fundamental aspect reflection upon the social world and the proper method of its description or explanation that contradictions should arise. That is, basic tensions in social science methodology (objectivism/subjectivism; positivism/humanism; structuralism/phenomenology...) are the products of a particular style or technique of philosophical practice. And this style is imbued with both a variety of differences such as contradictions, paradoxes, dilemmas, dualisms, binary oppositions as well as with attempts to suture these incongruities into what can seem like a unitary theory.","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/10350339109360344","pdf":"","k":["Objectivism","Epistemology","Subjectivism","Positivism","Structuralism (philosophy of science)","Unitary state","Binary opposition","Sociology"]},{"doi":"10.1080/10350339109360340","t":"Discerning the discerning traveller","a":["Glenn Stillar"],"d":"1991-01-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/10350339109360340","pdf":"","k":["Applied linguistics","Linguistics","Spring (device)","Sociology","Philosophy","Engineering"]},{"doi":"10.1080/10350339109360343","t":"Drama, performance, praxis","a":["David Birch"],"d":"1991-01-01","abs":"","oa":"closed","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/10350339109360343","pdf":"","k":["Praxis","Drama","Sociology","Linguistics","Literature","Art","Philosophy","Epistemology"]}]